# ── Construction Cam — Environment Variables ──────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to understand what secrets are needed.
# NEVER create a real .env file — all secrets go into GitHub Repository Secrets.
#
# GitHub Repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions → New repository secret
#
# ── Required ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# WebRTC signaling server URL (your Render.com deployment)
# Example: wss://webrtc-signaling-server-xxxx.onrender.com
SIGNALING_URL=wss://YOUR-SERVER.onrender.com

# TURN servers JSON array (Metered.ca credentials)
# Get from: https://dashboard.metered.ca → Your App → TURN Credentials → Show ICE Servers
# Paste the entire JSON array as a single line string
# Example:
# TURN_SERVERS=[{"urls":"stun:standard.relay.metered.ca:80"},{"urls":"turn:standard.relay.metered.ca:80","username":"YOUR_USER","credential":"YOUR_PASS"},{"urls":"turn:standard.relay.metered.ca:80?transport=tcp","username":"YOUR_USER","credential":"YOUR_PASS"},{"urls":"turn:standard.relay.metered.ca:443","username":"YOUR_USER","credential":"YOUR_PASS"},{"urls":"turns:standard.relay.metered.ca:443?transport=tcp","username":"YOUR_USER","credential":"YOUR_PASS"}]
TURN_SERVERS=[{"urls":"stun:standard.relay.metered.ca:80"},{"urls":"turn:standard.relay.metered.ca:80","username":"YOUR_USER","credential":"YOUR_PASS"}]

# ── Optional (future milestones) ──────────────────────────────────────────────

# Multiset VPS API key (M5)
# MULTISET_API_KEY=

# Sentry DSN for error tracking (M7)
# SENTRY_DSN=

# ── How to update credentials ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Go to GitHub repo → Settings → Secrets and variables → Actions
# 2. Click the secret name → Update
# 3. Paste new value → Save
# 4. Push any file or manually trigger the workflow
# 5. Done — new credentials deployed, old ones never existed in code
